# Express controllers

## Router (`backend/routers/`)

- Map HTTP method + path to a controller function
- Attach middleware chains only (`requireAuth`, `requireVerifiedEmail`, `optionalAuth`)
- No business logic, Prisma calls, or inline `async (req, res)` handlers

```typescript
authRouter.post('/password-change', requireAuth, changePasswordController);
```

## Controller (`backend/controllers/{domain}/`)

- One exported `*Controller` per route action in `{action}.controller.ts`
- Aggregate in `{domain}Controllers.ts` and export a `controllers` object (mealstogo-style barrel)
- Re-export from `controllers/{domain}/index.ts`

```typescript
// backend/controllers/auth/authControllers.ts
export const controllers = {
  postRegister: registerController,
  postLogin: loginController,
  getMe: meController,
};

// backend/routers/authRouter.ts
import { controllers } from '../controllers/auth/authControllers';

authRouter.post('/register', controllers.postRegister);
```

## Handler rules

1. Parse input with `@repo/api` Zod schemas
2. Respond via `sendApiSuccess` / `sendApiError` or `throw new ApiError(...)`
3. Always `next(error)` in `catch` — never inline `res.status(500).json(...)`
4. Auth via middleware on the router; do not accept session tokens in request body
5. Side effects (mailer, bcrypt, Prisma) live in controllers or `backend/services/` — never in `@repo/api`

## Services (`backend/services/`)

Extract shared logic only when reused by 2+ controllers (e.g. mailer helpers in `backend/lib/mailer/`).

